{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792103411,"nonce":"d12QHA2FoIXn3g91AqiIlBvNNks=","title":"Array for loops reevaluate the source expression","message":"The array loop desugaring clones the source expression into length and element access without storing its value. A source() returning [1,2,3] is called four times instead of once. TestUnicode teardown iterates FileSystem.readDirectory while deleting entries, so repeated reads skip files and eventually yield null; Path.join then yields the directory itself and deleteFile fails. Cache the source before the loop and use that reference for length and element access. Reproducer: /tmp/rayzor-sys-next/ArrayIterationSource.hx.","files":null}]}